course: dictionary
lesson: 9230
title: Sonar: listening with sound
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sonar is a way of finding things under water. It sends out sound waves and listens for their echoes. «Sonar sends sound pulses down and listens for echoes from the seabed or fish.» The echo that comes back tells the sonar where something is.
explain: The word can also mean the machine that does this. «Ships use echoes under water, called sonar.» Ships and submarines use sonar to measure how deep the sea is, or to find fish and wrecks. When you read the word, check the sentence: is it talking about the method or the machine?
explain: Animals can do this too. Bats and dolphins use a natural kind of sonar called echolocation. «Dolphins and bats use echoes in a similar way.» The clue is in the word itself: they locate, or find, things by using echoes.
fact: Sonar means finding things under water by sending out sound and listening for the echo.
fact: Sonar can also mean the machine that ships and submarines use to do this.
fact: Echolocation is the natural kind of sonar used by bats and dolphins.
fact: Sound travels about four times faster in water than in air.
fact: The time an echo takes to come back tells you how far away something is.
exercise: «Sonar sends a ping and times the echo.» What does sonar time to work out the distance? | *The echo | The colour of the boat | The weather | The fish
exercise: «Ships use sonar to measure the depth of the sea.» What does a ship use sonar to measure? | The number of sailors | *The depth of the sea | The speed of the wind | The colour of the water
exercise: Find and copy the name of the natural kind of sonar used by bats and dolphins. | ultrasound | *echolocation | depth | ping
test: Which animals use echolocation? | Lions and tigers | Cats and horses | Ants and bees | *Bats and dolphins
test: «Sonar sends sound pulses down and listens for echoes.» Why does sonar listen? | To make the fish swim faster | To change the colour of the water | *To hear the echoes that bounce back | To stop the ship
exam: «Sound travels about four times faster in water than in air.» What is the name for a sound that bounces back after hitting something? | Splash | Glow | Shadow | *Echo
